  "description": "AFFECIO HACKS ’26 — by Affecio Welcome to AFFECIO HACKS ’26 — an online hackathon by Affecio, bringing together students, developers, designers, innovators, and problem-solvers to turn ideas into meaningful digital solutions. About the Opportunity AFFECIO HACKS ’26 is an online hackathon bringing together students and aspiring builders to solve real-world problems through technology, creativity, and collaboration. Participants can work individually or in teams to build a functional solution during the hackathon. Teams are encouraged to experiment with modern technologies, APIs, open-source tools, frameworks, and AI tools where permitted. The hackathon is designed to give participants hands-on experience in ideation, development, problem-solving, teamwork, and product building. Projects will be evaluated based on technical implementation, innovation, impact, UI/UX, and presentation. Challenge Tracks Human Connection Build technology that helps people connect, understand, support, and relate to one another. AI & Social Interaction Explore how AI can enable more meaningful, natural, and human-centered interactions. Communities Create tools that help people discover, build, and strengthen communities around shared interests. Communication Reimagine how people communicate, express themselves, and build relationships in the digital world. These are broad challenge themes. The actual problem statements will be revealed when the hackathon begins. Problem Statement Reveal The official problem statements will be revealed on 21 October 2026 , at the start of the hackathon. Participants will receive the specific challenges at the beginning of the build phase and can start working on their solutions from that point. No problem statement will be provided before the official reveal. ️ Hackathon Timeline 21 October 2026 — 9:30 AM IST Hackathon Begins + Problem Statement Reveal 21–28 October 2026 Build Phase 28 October 2026 — 9:30 PM IST ⏳ Build Phase Ends 28 October 2026 — 9:30–11:",
